    kind: "monograph",
    text: "Multifactorial ocular surface disease characterized by loss of tear film homeostasis, symptoms and tear instability, often with hyperosmolarity, inflammation, surface damage and neurosensory abnormalities.\nBurning, foreign body sensation, fluctuating vision, photophobia, staining, low TBUT, reduced Schirmer or hyperosmolarity depending on subtype.\nSymptom questionnaire, slit-lamp exam, tear break-up time, ocular surface staining, lid/MGD assessment, Schirmer when aqueous deficiency suspected, targeted testing when severe or discordant.\nEducation, environmental measures, lubricants, lid management, anti-inflammatory therapy when indicated, tear conservation, treatment of MGD, serum tears/scleral lenses for severe disease.\nSevere pain, unilateral marked redness, corneal ulcer, significant vision loss, cicatrization, suspicion of autoimmune disease or infection.",
